// R11 gap 4 (docs/OWNERSHIP.md, "Still broken" table, row 4): an `arc` local
// declared inside a block is never released, because the drop pass is
// function-scoped rather than block-scoped, so nothing schedules a release
// for a binding a nested block (here, a `while` body) pops before the
// function returns. Re-executing the block reassigns the same C-local
// variable to a fresh box each time, so the loop leaks every iteration.
//
// MEASURED 2026-09-08, and it corrects what this comment used to claim. The
// old text said the last iteration's box is released by a function-scoped
// drop at the end of `main`, which is why the count came out one short. That
// is FALSE: this program emits ZERO release calls of any kind (`cell emit ...
// | grep -c cell_arc_drop` is 0), so nothing is ever freed. An interposed
// malloc counter reports ALLOC=3000 FREE=0 LIVE=3000 for 1000 iterations at
// three allocations each. The `leaks -atExit` reading of 2997 is a
// conservative-scan artifact, not a release: the last iteration's
// allocations are still reachable from a stale stack/register slot when the
// scan runs. tools/check.sh's leak stage documents the mechanism and both
// recipes that prove it.
//
// This fixture ISOLATES that gap alone: `a` is boxed straight from a string
// literal (BOX, R11 retain rule 1), never touches a struct or a `shared`
// parameter, and is never reassigned as a `var` would be (that is the
// SEPARATE gap `reassigned_var.cell` measures). tools/check.sh's `leaks`
// stage pins the expected leak count; see that file for the number and the
// commit it was measured at.
//
// Status: parses, passes `cell check`. LLVM and MLIR refuse it (arc is
// scalar-first-refused there, same as examples/arc.cell), which the existing
// backend-agreement stage already tolerates for arc.cell; this file lives
// under examples/leaks/ specifically so it is invisible to the top-level
// examples/*.cell corpus, agreement, and mlir-lowering loops (see
// examples/leaks/README.md).

pub fn print_int(copy value: Int);

pub fn main() {
    var i = 0
    while i < 1000 {
        let arc a = "leaked-block-local"
        i = i + 1
    }
    print_int(i)
}
